  {
    "title": "Meshtastic Meetup",
    "slug": "sun-comm-meshtastic",
    "location": "Community Stage",
    "description": "Meshtastic is a free, open-source way to send messages and sensor data between small, low-power radios, with no cell plan or internet connection. In this talk you’ll see how a message hops across a mesh of radios, what the hardware looks like, and how the same network can carry weather readings, door-alarm alerts, GPS positions, and solar status. We’ll compare mesh with Wi-Fi, and cover what Meshtastic can’t do. You’ll leave knowing how to get your first radio on the air, and where to find us at MakerFX Makerspace in Orlando.",
    "date": "2026-11-08 15:30:00",
    "enddate": "2026-11-08 16:00:00",
